157
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:47,960
I told you it's...

158
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:48,160
Wait.

159
00:08:48,580 --> 00:08:48,760
Huh?

160
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:52,160
Your muscles are holding on to a lot of fatigue.

161
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:52,960
They are?

162
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:54,980
You're sore when you move, right?

163
00:08:55,780 --> 00:08:57,200
Yeah, but how could you tell?

164
00:08:58,340 --> 00:08:59,760
Because it's my gift.

165
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:00,920
Your gift?

166
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:02,580
Here, I'll make it better.

167
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,840
Song recovery magic.

168
00:09:06,220 --> 00:09:07,120
Healing lullaby.

169
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:10,600
So cool!

170
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:12,380
She's good.

171
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:17,480
It takes an incredibly delicate touch to direct magic with that much accuracy.

172
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:21,600
Well, how do you feel?

173
00:09:21,780 --> 00:09:22,580
I don't know.

174
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:24,520
Oh!

175
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:26,340
Whoa!

176
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:28,420
That's awesome!

177
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:30,880
I was sore all over and now I don't hurt anywhere!

178
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:32,760
My body feels so light!

179
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,020
Bye-bye muscle fatigue!

180
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:35,880
Whatever you did really worked!

181
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:37,140
You're amazing, Kahano!

182
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:38,400
It's like I have a whole new body!

183
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:41,160
I've never seen someone use song recovery magic before.

184
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:42,160
That's great!

185
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:43,420
I'm glad it worked out.

186
00:09:43,980 --> 00:09:45,960
Okay, that'll be a hundred yule, please.

187
00:09:46,260 --> 00:09:47,260
You're charging me?

188
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:48,340
Just kidding.

189
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:49,900
Oh, good.

190
00:09:50,140 --> 00:09:51,120
But not really!

191
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:52,380
Are you serious?

192
00:09:53,140 --> 00:09:54,760
Money's a big deal, you know.

193
00:09:55,540 --> 00:09:56,300
Take it.

194
00:09:56,700 --> 00:09:57,480
Great, thanks!

195
00:09:57,600 --> 00:10:01,140
And if you ever need another healing lullaby, I'm more than happy to help.

196
00:10:01,140 --> 00:10:03,520
I can't believe I just lost a hundred yule.

197
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:05,200
Please, that's nothing.

198
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:05,820
Nothing?

199
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:08,040
That much money went by ten pot potatoes!

200
00:10:08,340 --> 00:10:09,460
Like I said, nothing.

201
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:11,360
Royalty!

202
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:15,260
You two are so funny.

203
00:10:15,700 --> 00:10:16,600
How old are you?

204
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:18,020
Fifteen.

205
00:10:18,380 --> 00:10:18,940
Me too.

206
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:20,600
Wow, both of you?

207
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:21,440
That's crazy!

208
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:22,300
So am I!

209
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:23,100
Oh, really?

210
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:25,880
Well, now we definitely have to be friends.

211
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:27,380
Sure, sounds great.

212
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:28,800
You're pretty funny, too.

213
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:31,820
A friend who's a girl my own age?

214
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:32,980
That's new.

215
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:35,200
Fine!

216
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:37,500
If you insist, I suppose that would be acceptable.

217
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:39,780
I mean, I won't not be your friend.

218
00:10:42,420 --> 00:10:44,740
Sorry, I guess I got a little carried away.

219
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:45,660
Little!

220
